","Let the side length of the cube is $2$. The center of the cube is at the origin $(1, 1, 1)$. The center of the central sphere is at the center of the cube, which be located at $(1, 1, 1)$. Let the radius of each sphere be $r$. The central sphere has its center at $(1, 1, 1)$ and its radius is $r$.

The other sphere is tangent to three faces of the cube. Since the sphere is also touching the cube, its center is at $(r, r, r)$. The distance from the center of the cube to the center of this sphere is $r + r = 2r$. The distance from the center of the cube to the corner is $\sqrt{1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2} = \sqrt{3}$. The distance from the corner to the corner of the cube is $\sqrt{2} \times 2 = 2\sqrt{2}$.

The distance from the center of the cube to the center of the sphere is $\sqrt{(1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2} = \sqrt{3(1 - r)^2} = \sqrt{3} (1 - r)$. Since the sphere is tangent to the cube, its center is at $(r, r, r)$. The distance from the center of the cube to the center of this sphere is $r + r = 2r$. Thus, $\sqrt{3} (1 - r) = 2r$.

Solving for $r$:
$r - r\sqrt{3} = 2r$
$r = -\sqrt{3} r$
$r + \sqrt{3} r = 0$
