3. Magnetic fields in galaxy clusters: Magnetic fields can also influence the distribution of matter in galaxy clusters, which are the largest structures in the universe. They can help to heat up the gas in galaxy clusters, which can in turn affect the rate of star formation in the galaxies within the cluster.

In summary, cosmic magnetic fields play a significant role in the formation and evolution of galaxies. They influence the distribution of matter in various ways, such as affecting star formation, shaping the structure of galaxies, and driving galactic jets and outflows. Further research is needed to fully understand the role of cosmic magnetic fields in the formation and evolution of galaxies.
