- Convective heat transfer coefficient \( h = 56.8 \, \text{W/m}^2K \)  

#### (i) Time to reach 50°C  
The time constant \( \tau \) is given by:  
\[
\tau = \frac{k \cdot t}{h \cdot A}
\]  
where \( t \) is the characteristic length. The characteristic length is the reciprocal of the volume-to-surface area ratio:  
\[
t = \frac{V}{A} = \frac{m}{\rho A} = \frac{1.2}{7150 \times 0.075} = 0.019 \, \text{m}
\]  
Now, the time constant is:  
\[
