<start_of_turn>model
","To find the gas pressure in cylinder B, we analyze the forces acting on the piston. The pressure balance equation is:

\[
P_A A_A + P_B A_B = P_0 A_A + m g
\]

Where:
- \( P_A = 500 \text{ kPa} \) (pressure in cylinder A)
- \( A_A = \pi (d_A/2)^2 = \pi (0.1/2)^2 = 0.007854 \text{ m}^2 \) (area of cylinder A)
- \( P_B = 100 \text{ kPa} \) (pressure in cylinder B)
- \( A_B = \pi (d_B/2)^2 = \pi (0.025/2)^2 = 0.0001963 \text{ m}^2 \) (area of cylinder B)
- \( P_0 = 100 \text{ kPa} \) (atmospheric pressure)
- \( m = 25 \text{ kg} \) (mass of the piston)
- \( g = 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2 \) (acceleration due to gravity)

Substituting the values:

\[
500 \times 0.007854 + P_B \times 0.0001963 = 100 \times 0.007854 + 25 \times 9.807
\]

Solving for \( P_B \):

\[
3.927 + 0.0001963 P_B = 0.7854 + 245.175
\]

\[
0.0001963 P_B = 245.175 - 3.927 + 0.7854
\]

\[
0.0001963 P_B = 242.933
\]

\[
P_B = \frac{242.933}{0.0001963} \approx 1230,000 \text{ Pa}
\]

\[
P_B \approx 1.230 \text{ MPa}
\]

Thus, the gas pressure in cylinder B is \(\boxed{1.23 \text{ MPa}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
