\[
v(t) = \frac{C_L}{C}
\]
Given \( v(t) = 10e^{-4t} \, \text{V} \), we can solve for \( C_L \):
\[
C_L = C v(t) = C \times 10e^{-4t}
\]
The energy stored in the capacitor is:
\[
W_L = \frac{1}{2} C \times C_L = \frac{1}{2} C \times C_L = \frac{1}{2} C \times C_L
\]
