1. A gas is composed of molecules that are in free motion (free to move freely with no intermolecular forces).  
2. The molecules are in random motion and move in random directions.  
3. The kinetic energy of the molecules is directly proportional to the temperature of the gas.  
4. The molecules are in free path (i.e., they do not collide with each other).  

