The curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y) = (u_x(x, y), u_y(x, y), 0)\) is given by:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \right) u_z - \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \right) u_y + \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \right) u_y.
\]
Substituting the components of \(\mathbf{V}\), we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \right) 0 - \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \right) u_y + \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \right) u_y.
\]
Simplifying, we get:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = 0 - 0 + \left( \frac{\partial}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \right) u_y = \frac{\partial u_y}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u_y}{\partial y}.
\]
Thus, the curl of \(\mathbf{V}\) is:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial u_y}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial u_y}{\partial y} \right) \hat{k}.
